00:54:00.400 --> 00:54:01.233
They get caught.

00:54:01.233 --> 00:54:03.020
It's not that they're
bad, it's that they get

00:54:03.020 --> 00:54:04.170
into their own dynamics.

00:54:04.170 --> 00:54:06.790
They go inside, they don't
become consumer centric.

00:54:06.790 --> 00:54:08.500
I think if you keep
reading those comments,

00:54:08.500 --> 00:54:10.700
keep engaging with it,
keep putting up content,

00:54:10.700 --> 00:54:13.860
you'll be unbelievably stunned on how easy

00:54:13.860 --> 00:54:15.810
the answers will come of what to do

00:54:15.810 --> 00:54:20.003
because it's been said to
you in the trenches, got it?

00:54:21.006 --> 00:54:21.839
What do you got Charly?

00:54:21.839 --> 00:54:24.650
- I admire you because
your network is so huge

00:54:24.650 --> 00:54:28.830
and I feel like everybody
is, oh, I've exchanged

00:54:28.830 --> 00:54:31.690
a DM with Gary before,
oh I've seen him here.

00:54:31.690 --> 00:54:34.260
It's like everybody knows
you and has had maybe some

00:54:34.260 --> 00:54:36.570
type of interaction with you,
although it may be small,

00:54:36.570 --> 00:54:41.080
but you just seem to be able
to create such a network

00:54:41.080 --> 00:54:44.070
and keep it, whereas I feel
like I could meet someone

00:54:44.070 --> 00:54:46.320
who I'm like, oh my god,
I met this girl yesterday,

00:54:46.320 --> 00:54:47.447
she was awesome, I wanna
grab dinner with her,

00:54:47.447 --> 00:54:49.120
and a week later I'm like,
oops, I forgot all about it.

00:54:49.120 --> 00:54:52.220
- Like, who was that blonde?

00:54:52.220 --> 00:54:53.327
- I don't even have that
many people in my life

00:54:53.327 --> 00:54:56.950
but you have millions and
you manage to curate these

00:54:56.950 --> 00:54:59.450
relationships with them and
keep them going and building

00:54:59.450 --> 00:55:02.158
them and it's almost overwhelming to me.

00:55:02.158 --> 00:55:05.480
- I think, much like anything
else, every one of us

00:55:05.480 --> 00:55:07.470
does something that is
overwhelming to each other.

00:55:07.470 --> 00:55:09.470
For me, people have always come natural.

00:55:10.662 --> 00:55:12.245
It's funny, if you think about earlier,

00:55:12.245 --> 00:55:13.078
10 minutes ago what I was

00:55:13.078 --> 00:55:14.750
talking about with people interaction,

00:55:14.750 --> 00:55:18.253
it's crazy because my love
in life is other people.

00:55:19.100 --> 00:55:22.100
It's probably why I got
to, respect isn't the eye

00:55:22.100 --> 00:55:24.719
or the shake, it's the truth, you know.

00:55:24.719 --> 00:55:28.240
My truth is, I really like people.

00:55:28.240 --> 00:55:31.890
And it starts with, closest
to the sun, like I would die

00:55:31.890 --> 00:55:33.640
for my family and then out from that.

00:55:33.640 --> 00:55:35.910
I think my employees
in here will tell you,

00:55:35.910 --> 00:55:37.806
there's just a different
level of how I manage it,

00:55:37.806 --> 00:55:39.400
I just like them more.

00:55:39.400 --> 00:55:40.670
I don't know what else to really, it's not

00:55:40.670 --> 00:55:43.390
super complicated, I want
to be admired and liked,

00:55:43.390 --> 00:55:47.050
I like and admire them, I give
respect right off the bat,

00:55:47.050 --> 00:55:49.050
you have to lose it, it's not
like you've gotta earn it,

00:55:49.050 --> 00:55:51.435
it's that lack of ego that
I think, I have so much

00:55:51.435 --> 00:55:55.010
confidence and bravado and
personality pours one way,

00:55:55.010 --> 00:55:58.870
but I think in my actions
I really, the thing I'm

00:55:58.870 --> 00:56:01.000
proud of is my ability to have humility,

00:56:01.000 --> 00:56:05.300
because honestly, I think
everything I've done

00:56:05.300 --> 00:56:06.900
yesterday back, it means nothing.

00:56:06.900 --> 00:56:08.965
It's very weird, it really works for me.

00:56:08.965 --> 00:56:13.965
I get it, I'm in the reverse,
I don't romanticize the back.

00:56:17.177 --> 00:56:20.190
It's probably why I push
against this, I'm even like

00:56:20.190 --> 00:56:21.870
psychoanalyzing myself right
now, I'm like, oh shit,

00:56:21.870 --> 00:56:22.720
that makes sense.

00:56:23.790 --> 00:56:28.790
I think people are 100%, the why of life.

00:56:29.088 --> 00:56:32.580
Starting with the people
that come to your funeral.

00:56:32.580 --> 00:56:34.460
Think about it, start with the end.

00:56:34.460 --> 00:56:37.290
Like, who'd you compel enough that, like,

00:56:37.290 --> 00:56:38.970
do you know why I think
going to a funeral is like

00:56:38.970 --> 00:56:41.250
the most fascinating thing in society?

00:56:41.250 --> 00:56:43.470
Because I'm surprised the
funerals I was willing

00:56:43.470 --> 00:56:45.320
to not go to.

00:56:45.320 --> 00:56:46.750
I'm being very real with everybody.

00:56:46.750 --> 00:56:50.470
I'm fascinated by some
of the people that I did

00:56:50.470 --> 00:56:51.910
business with, in the liquor business

00:56:51.910 --> 00:56:53.830
over the last 20 years, I
was very young, I was a kid,

00:56:53.830 --> 00:56:55.140
and like kind of like you know,

00:56:55.140 --> 00:56:56.690
a generational family business.

00:56:58.090 --> 00:57:00.310
I think it's very interesting, in a world

00:57:00.310 --> 00:57:01.929
where we're all selfish
and doing our thing,

00:57:01.929 --> 00:57:05.868
who's brought you so much
value that you'll just stop.

00:57:05.868 --> 00:57:08.873
Obviously your family
members, but then what?

00:57:09.890 --> 00:57:11.210
Like, right?

00:57:11.210 --> 00:57:13.155
It's just super interesting.

00:57:13.155 --> 00:57:13.988
I've basically been living my life

00:57:13.988 --> 00:57:14.980
for a pretty long time now

00:57:14.980 --> 00:57:18.830
on can I be so great that everybody stops

00:57:18.830 --> 00:57:20.800
and comes to my funeral?

00:57:20.800 --> 00:57:22.110
You know, it's funny,
I've always been like,

00:57:22.110 --> 00:57:23.896
for a long time I never talked about it,

00:57:23.896 --> 00:57:25.025
and then I talked about it, I'm like,

00:57:25.025 --> 00:57:27.056
is that douchy, what is that?

00:57:27.056 --> 00:57:28.600
Now I'm kind of like, I'm
super happy I'm like that.

00:57:28.600 --> 00:57:31.372
It means I want to do the right thing

00:57:31.372 --> 00:57:33.100
for the right reasons.

00:57:33.100 --> 00:57:36.890
Not to make up what respect
and admiration and kindness is,

00:57:36.890 --> 00:57:40.100
but the actual truth behind it.

00:57:40.100 --> 00:57:44.450
So yeah, I value, and I'm
also grateful, you know,

00:57:44.450 --> 00:57:47.514
I'm actually listening to all three of you

00:57:47.514 --> 00:57:49.840
because of what you wanted
to do, there was always

00:57:49.840 --> 00:57:51.660
a thought if you guys
became big time drivers,

00:57:51.660 --> 00:57:54.650
if you got on television,
you knew that you would

00:57:54.650 --> 00:57:56.845
have some level of fame.

00:57:56.845 --> 00:57:59.800
Whether you dreamed about it,
for TV you dreamed about it,

00:57:59.800 --> 00:58:01.960
for you, it could have been
a little bit different,

00:58:01.960 --> 00:58:03.390
but you just knew you'd be known.

00:58:03.390 --> 00:58:05.840
For me I always wanted
to be a business man.

00:58:05.840 --> 00:58:08.430
And that didn't mean that
anybody would ever know you.

00:58:08.430 --> 00:58:11.650
So for me, all this
attention came when I was

00:58:11.650 --> 00:58:15.129
not looking for it and I
was well into my late 30s

00:58:15.129 --> 00:58:17.180
when it became like, oh,
this is gonna get like,

00:58:17.180 --> 00:58:19.420
I think I'm gonna be the next Oprah.

00:58:19.420 --> 00:58:21.150
In like white dude form.

00:58:21.150 --> 00:58:26.010
So there's a level of
gratitude that makes me,

00:58:26.010 --> 00:58:29.450
the fact that people wanna know who I am

00:58:29.450 --> 00:58:31.950
seems weird and amazing and all of that.

00:58:33.052 --> 00:58:34.650
What do you got, bro?

00:58:34.650 --> 00:58:38.990
- I think for me, I have probably a basic

00:58:38.990 --> 00:58:39.823
question for you.

00:58:39.823 --> 00:58:41.030
- [Gary] Cool, basic's good.

00:58:42.260 --> 00:58:44.010
- We have so many sponsors
and so many people we're

00:58:44.010 --> 00:58:46.149
trying to make happy and that's all right,

00:58:46.149 --> 00:58:48.590
it's what makes our world go
'round, how do we support them

00:58:48.590 --> 00:58:52.143
and show them on social media
without looking, cheese?

00:58:53.608 --> 00:58:54.850
What they want, and what
I want to post is very--

00:58:54.850 --> 00:58:57.790
- Your basic question is
actually the question,

00:58:57.790 --> 00:58:58.910
so good job.

00:58:58.910 --> 00:59:00.530
I think it's communication.

00:59:00.530 --> 00:59:03.600
I think, first of all,
right now you're young

00:59:03.600 --> 00:59:05.583
and the leverage you have
is different than say

00:59:05.583 --> 00:59:09.607
a top five racer, 10, 15
years in with championships,

00:59:09.607 --> 00:59:12.220
but it will always be communication.

00:59:12.220 --> 00:59:15.030
I think, whether it's
your makeup at this young

00:59:15.030 --> 00:59:16.360
of an age or when you have the leverage.

00:59:16.360 --> 00:59:18.810
The right answer is,
hey, you're my sponsor.

00:59:18.810 --> 00:59:21.320
You want me to do good for
you, I don't want to do

00:59:21.320 --> 00:59:22.770
what you want me to do on social,

00:59:22.770 --> 00:59:25.150
which then means it's
going to feel inauthentic,

00:59:25.150 --> 00:59:26.920
which then means it's dead.

00:59:26.920 --> 00:59:30.100
If I had never worn a pair
of K-Swiss when I was a kid,

00:59:30.100 --> 00:59:31.650
I would never have done the collaboration.

00:59:31.650 --> 00:59:33.400
Thank God, I mean this, this is not a joke

00:59:33.400 --> 00:59:36.170
because I would have wanted
to, thank god I had one,

00:59:36.170 --> 00:59:37.710
and I've been trying
to think and I've still

00:59:37.710 --> 00:59:39.930
been battling with my head,
I'm trying to find Andy,

00:59:39.930 --> 00:59:41.730
Andy Greco, if you're watching this,

00:59:41.730 --> 00:59:43.380
sixth grade when you wore those

00:59:43.380 --> 00:59:46.790
weird red sneakers with
leafs on them and I made

00:59:46.790 --> 00:59:48.435
fun of you and I apologize for that,

00:59:48.435 --> 00:59:51.640
did I have K-Swiss or was that Adidas?

00:59:51.640 --> 00:59:53.340
I need your help on that
because I can't remember.

00:59:53.340 --> 00:59:55.130
But I definitely remember the one K-Swiss

00:59:55.130 --> 00:59:56.560
tennis sneakers I had.

00:59:56.560 --> 00:59:58.030
I think authenticity matters.

00:59:58.030 --> 00:59:59.700
Now you don't have say the way that I do,

00:59:59.700 --> 01:00:01.480
and so you've got a sponsor
too that maybe isn't

01:00:01.480 --> 01:00:04.635
your favorite power
drink or what have you.

01:00:04.635 --> 01:00:07.040
What I think it is, is authenticity.

01:00:07.040 --> 01:00:08.760
One, I think you need to be posting

01:00:08.760 --> 01:00:09.710
what you want to be posting.

01:00:09.710 --> 01:00:11.760
Obviously you need to be able to deal

01:00:11.760 --> 01:00:13.820
with the ramifications,
like if you say things

01:00:13.820 --> 01:00:16.090
that are not going to fly
you'll have to deal with that.

01:00:16.090 --> 01:00:20.343
But I think when you're
obligated to do a post,

01:00:21.195 --> 01:00:24.110
like, ready, Macho Man's
my favorite wrestler.

01:00:24.110 --> 01:00:26.950
If I had to post this I
would do some sort of post

01:00:26.950 --> 01:00:29.420
that'd be like a weird
face, and in my copy

01:00:29.420 --> 01:00:31.610
I'd be like, here's my
Ultimate Warrior story.

01:00:31.610 --> 01:00:33.700
Number one, when he beat Macho Man,

01:00:33.700 --> 01:00:35.650
I fucking hated him for it.

01:00:35.650 --> 01:00:38.950
Number two, I loved him as
the Dingo Warrior in his

01:00:38.950 --> 01:00:41.160
battles with Rick Rude in the Texas League

01:00:41.160 --> 01:00:44.480
that later went to the,
like, I would tell the truth.

01:00:44.480 --> 01:00:49.480
And so that's, you know,
there's people in sports

01:00:50.035 --> 01:00:53.140
that are being represented
or have sponsorship deals

01:00:53.140 --> 01:00:56.990
with a product that they, for
example, we work with Pepsi,

01:00:56.990 --> 01:00:58.870
and I told Pepsi, and
say it loud right now,

01:00:58.870 --> 01:01:00.960
they're currently a multi
million dollar client,

01:01:00.960 --> 01:01:02.620
I grew up drinking Coke.

01:01:02.620 --> 01:01:05.650
I just think the truth
is always the leverage.

01:01:05.650 --> 01:01:08.640
My K-Swiss deal, my
sneaker deal, almost died

01:01:08.640 --> 01:01:10.640
because in the clause I would not sign

01:01:10.640 --> 01:01:13.150
that I would only wear K-Swiss
even though they give me

01:01:13.150 --> 01:01:14.060
millions of dollars.

01:01:14.060 --> 01:01:15.320
- They make the tubes?

01:01:15.320 --> 01:01:16.420
K-Swiss, is that them?

01:01:16.420 --> 01:01:17.400
- What's that, the tubes?

01:01:17.400 --> 01:01:19.850
- [Erik] Yeah, the shoes,
with tubes on the bottom.

01:01:19.850 --> 01:01:20.766
You know what I'm talking about?

01:01:20.766 --> 01:01:21.599
- No, I'm trying to think though.

01:01:21.599 --> 01:01:22.432
I don't think so, what are the tubes?

